        {
            "number": 8,
            "revision": "25d792c458bd2b1941b32e329de48fa74d1c82aa",
            "parents": [
                "3ea5c2f28f576068b7e0135507ad809bdeb1cd9b"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/45/82445/8",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "createdOn": 1755853704,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Since the patch has been pending for a while, just a friendly ping as a reminder for review."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Josh Lehan",
                        "email": "krellan@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Krellan"
                    },
                    "message": "I can't give +2 because I don't have that permission in this repository, so somebody else will have to give +2"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Does the sensor name match to (par of) a D-Bus sensor object?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "For example, in the case of a PLDM sensor, if the object in the PLDM tree is `/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/temperature/SENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_5_DIMM_A0_TEMP_C`, \nthen it should display the sensor name as `SENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_5_DIMM_A0_TEMP_C`.\nOn our platform, in conjunction with [Gerrit 82447] for `phosphor-pid-control`, the demo would look like this:\n```\nroot@bmc:~# busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.State.FanCtrl \n/xyz/openbmc_project/settings/fanctrl/zone0 xyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone \nFailSafeSensorsa{ss} 18 \"SENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_5_DIMM_A0_TEMP_C\" \"Sensor reading bad\" \n\"SENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_5_DIMM_A10_TEMP_C\" \"Sensor reading bad\"...\n```\nThis output shows a list of sensor names such as \"SENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_5_DIMM_A0_TEMP_C\", each associated with a status like \"Sensor reading bad\".\n\n[Gerrit 82447]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/82447"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is string better than en enum here? Several existing PDIs use enums to expose failure states."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Since sensor names may vary across platforms, it's not suitable to predefine them using enums. However, using enums for failure reasons should be acceptable. I can first try to see if it's possible to convert just the reason part to an enum while still displaying both the sensor name and reason in a dictionary type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019ve already tried converting the property to use enums. The output looks like this:\n```\nroot@bmc:~# busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.State.FanCtrl \n/xyz/openbmc_project/settings/fanctrl/zone0 \nxyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone \nFailSafeSensors\na{ss} 95 \"MEDUSA_MB8_HSC_12V_TEMP_C\" \n\"xyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone.FailureReason.MissingSensor\" \n...\nSENTINEL_DOME_SLOT_7_MB_X8_RTM_TEMP_C\" \n\"xyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone.FailureReason.BadReading\"\n...\n```\nHowever, this approach no longer directly displays the human-readable reason strings like those used in `phosphor-pid-control`. May I ask which format you would prefer to see?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I wouls use errors documented in the PDI repo."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "To ensure I implement this exactly as you expect, could you please confirm the desired for FailureReason?\n\nOption 1 (enum): keep enum; busctl shows fully-qualified enum names (e.g., xyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone.FailureReason.Timeout).\nOption 2 (strings): return Common errors directly (e.g., xyz.openbmc_project.Common.Error.Timeout).\n\nFor domain-specific reasons without a direct Common error (MarginHot, ThresholdAsserted, BadReading), should we:\nkeep them as enum values (and, if a string is needed, map to Common.Error.Unknown), or remap to the closest Common errors (e.g., InvalidArgument / InternalFailure)?\n\nAlso, should we rename enum values to match Common terms (ObjectMissing\u2192ResourceNotFound, NotFunctional\u2192InternalFailure)?\n\nOr is the intention to define these errors in a newly created Zone.error.yaml? I\u2019d really appreciate it if you could share more detailed thoughts to help clarify.\n\nThank you for your guidance."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I would vote for defining errors in the Zone.error.yaml (for the ones that don't map clearly to existing errors). Enum to string mapping can be done by consuming apps. Bmcweb does this, for eg, where it converts the PDI enums to Redfish messages."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Josh Lehan",
                        "email": "krellan@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Krellan"
                    },
                    "message": "I also vote for defining errors here in `Debug.Pid.Zone.FailureReason`, to avoid loss of information by trying to map errors to their `Common` equivalents (which are not always adequate to express the richness of information we need to convey here). I like the idea of printing the fully qualified enum name. Localization to more human-readable text should be done in the UI/presentation layer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Apologies \u2014 I\u2019m a bit confused and would like to reconfirm:\n\nMy understanding is that `FailSafeSensors` is a property, so its `FailureReason` enum should remain in `Debug.Pid.Zone.interface.yaml`. In contrast, `errors.yaml` files (e.g., `Zone.errors.yaml`) are for defining D-Bus error types that can be thrown by methods, not for defining property enums. Based on that, there should be no further changes needed to the PDI interface in this patchset, and `Zone.errors.yaml` would only be added later if we introduce Zone methods that need domain-specific errors \u2014 is that correct?\n\nSeparately, should I update phosphor-pid-control to store failure reasons internally as the `Debug.Pid.Zone.FailureReason` enum (instead of strings), and only convert them to human-readable strings when writing to the journal?\n\nThank you all once again for your guidance!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "So, my understanding is that for this patch, I should keep the current changes, and then add a commit in `phosphor-pid-control` to update all fail sensor reasons to use the defined `FailureReason` enum instead of strings. After that, I would adjust patch [82447] accordingly to align with the new approach.\n\nIf I\u2019ve misunderstood, please let me know. Thank you!\n\n[82447]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/82447"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "In [85920], I\u2019ve already updated `phosphor-pid-control`\u2019s internal fail reason handling to rely on the `FailureReason` enum defined in this patch, and made the corresponding changes in [82447].\n\nIf there\u2019s anything else that needs to be corrected, please let me know.\n\n[85920]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/85920\n[82447]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-pid-control/+/82447"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "What is expected to happen in case of a BMC reboot?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Debug/Pid/Zone.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I expect that regardless of whether it's a BMC reboot or any other operation, the `xyz.openbmc_project.Debug.Pid.Zone` interface and its `FailSafeSensors` property will only be created after phosphor-pid-control has completed building the zone and created the object `/xyz/openbmc_project/settings/fanctrl/zone<id>`"
                }
            ],
